    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0555" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1812⅖</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-07">July 7, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The more I think of it the more I feel that we should say nothing about the Near
                    East or Palestine or the Arabs at this time.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d653-f1"/> If
                    we pat either group on the back, we automatically stir up trouble at a <pb
                        facs="0556" n="544" xml:id="pg544"/> critical moment. Furthermore, the
                    question of arms for Palestine ought not to be mentioned because it is
                    impossible from the military point of view to get them just now.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d653-f1" n="12" xml:id="d653-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding a separate proposal for the issuance of a
                    declaration of policy by this Government with respect to the Near East, see <ref
                        target="#pg24">pp. 24</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
